\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\section{Notation}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
\hline
Symbol & Meaning \\
\hline
$\alpha$ & regularization coefficient \\
$\beta$ & momentum coefficient \\
$\gamma$ & discount factor \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\section{Algorithm}
The learning rate $\alpha$ controls the update magnitude, and we decay $\alpha$ every ten epochs.
The decay rate $\beta$ multiplies the step size, while $\gamma$ discounts future rewards.
Later the momentum coefficient $\beta$ smooths the gradient estimate.
The step size $\delta$ bounds the line search.
\section{Discussion}
Tuning $\alpha$ and $\beta$ jointly matters most in practice.
\end{document}

